seg-22eb5bd00092 = Purpose

# text
seg-25678ae41147 = Public material describes a lunar south-pole reference station that monitors a lunar navigation service, computes local differential corrections, keeps a lunar time reference on an atomic clock, and carries a laser retroreflector and a VLBI transmitter for the lunar reference frame (the class publicly described for ESA's NovaMoon concept; sources below). Kshana already models each piece separately. This study composes them into one reproducible, open analysis of what such a station could do under public assumptions, and pre-registers it so it can be scored against published results and, eventually, flight results.

