seg-f034e2642dab = For a differential reference station at a known south-polar site: at each user point on a ring grid from { "80" }° S to the pole and over the region, across a day of epochs and Monte Carlo trials, the percentile corrected and uncorrected position error (3-D, horizontal, vertical), availability with a reason for every unavailable epoch, coverage against a threshold stated before the run, DO-229E protection levels, the coverage radius per azimuth sector, and the correction-link budget at the station and at the worst point. No new physics: it sweeps the tested functions of <c1/> and reduces to that kind exactly at one point, one epoch and one trial.

