seg-10a1d62ab5cc = <c1/> runs the bundled inputs on a { "2" }° grid with { "100" } trials and the DEM horizon at every site. The station site ({ "89" }° S, { "0" }° E) has a highest horizon of about { "4.0" }°, below the { "5" }° mask, so at the station the terrain does not bind; at the user points the area-weighted mean of each point's highest horizon is { "9.7" }° and the largest { "26.3" }°. Against the same inputs with the flat mask, the region's corrected p95 3-D error rises from { "16.3" } m to { "18.6" } m and the largest HPL from { "480" } m to { "62" } km. Region availability rises from { "91.9" } % to { "93.0" } %: an epoch is unavailable when a point uses a satellite the station does not see, and a horizon that hides that satellite from the point can make the epoch available.

