seg-6d18d8a8dc78 = <b>Terrain and horizon masking: addressed in { "0.36" }, with limits.</b> Per-site horizon masks from a stated profile or the vendored LOLA DEM crop are modelled (above). What remains: the vendored crop is { "1200" } m per pixel, so relief below about a kilometre is smoothed away and block means lower sharp peaks; a ray that leaves the crop (about { "420" } km from the pole) ends there; there is no diffraction, terrain multipath or partial obstruction; site positions for ranging stay on the mean sphere at the stated heights (the DEM sets the horizon only); the horizon is not validated against an external figure. The per-satellite export site of <c1/> is masked like a grid point: with a <c2/> section each export row carries <c3/> and the report the site's horizon (<c4/>); the antenna in-beam tallies still count every link that clears the flat mask.

