seg-5bba9be34cad = <b>Solution style (filter, height constraint, three satellites): an opt-in in { "0.36" }, with limits.</b> A <c1/> section (<c2/>) adds a height pseudo-measurement, a three-satellite minimum with it, and a static-user weighted least-squares window over epochs (a shared position, a clock per epoch), which stands in for a filter. What remains: it treats the epochs' errors as independent, so it averages down faster than errors correlated in time would; it is static-user only; there is no dynamic filter, carrier phase or ambiguity resolution; the case trace (<c3/>) shows the snapshot arithmetic. The published-claims addendum with this mode is <c4/> (pre-registered alone). With a { "1" } m height constraint, three satellites and a 6-epoch window (ILLUSTRATIVE settings), the R300 corrected p95 3-D error falls from { "280.6" } m to { "2.11" } m (horizontal { "0.90" } m, not scored); K1 to K5 still fail and K6 passes, { "1" } of { "6" } as in the recorded run. The window's independence assumption favours it.

